     The sources available from linc.cis.upenn.edu contain everything
that's needed to build on VMS [except a C compiler :-].  The build
procedure does use an object library--one which it creates when it's
executed.  The only time it would be missing would be if someone tried
to link without compiling first...

     Prebuilt binaries for VMS are available via anonymous FTP from host
uars.acd.ucar.edu in directory [.SRC.NETHACK].  See the file there called
NETHACK.README for details.  Those same files are available via DECnet on
SPAN from ACDURS::SYS$LCL:[SRC.NETHACK] (if not already defined, ACDURS
has address 9.367 or 9583).

